{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1436092,
  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197378",
      "title": "Optimizing Lists with FlatList",
      "lectureOrder": 26,
      "videoOrder": 23,
      "sourceHash": "166a147fe461977e5aaa46481c2afbafffb97363053ffa4074b5b41b4e97083d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.68,
          "en": "So we got our scrollable list here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.68,
          "end": 7.513,
          "en": "and this is implemented with this ScrollView.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.47,
          "end": 10.67,
          "en": "Now, this solution has one downside,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.67,
          "end": 13.187,
          "en": "one disadvantage though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.187,
          "end": 14.51,
          "en": "ScrollView is great,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.51,
          "end": 18.02,
          "en": "if you wanna add scrolling around some content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.02,
          "end": 19.99,
          "en": "For example, if you had an article,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.99,
          "end": 22.41,
          "en": "which would be too long to fit on a screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.41,
          "end": 23.79,
          "en": "or you simply don't know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.79,
          "end": 26.63,
          "en": "which device sizes your users will be using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.63,
          "end": 29.48,
          "en": "and you wanna make sure that an article for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.48,
          "end": 30.97,
          "en": "is scrollable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.97,
          "end": 34.6,
          "en": "In such situations, ScrollView is perfect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.6,
          "end": 39.12,
          "en": "For lists as we have it here, it's not perfect though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.12,
          "end": 40.66,
          "en": "The reason for that is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.66,
          "end": 44.62,
          "en": "that lists like this could become very long.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.62,
          "end": 49.43,
          "en": "Sure, you might only have like 10 or 20 items on there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.43,
          "end": 51.52,
          "en": "And especially for such a goal list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.52,
          "end": 54.87,
          "en": "it's very likely that you have around that size",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.87,
          "end": 57.35,
          "en": "or around that amount of items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.35,
          "end": 59.04,
          "en": "But you could also have lists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.04,
          "end": 62.203,
          "en": "with hundreds or thousands of items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.18,
          "end": 65.61,
          "en": "Now, what ScrollView does is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.61,
          "end": 69.69,
          "en": "it always renders all the items that are inside of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.69,
          "end": 72.62,
          "en": "whenever the overall UI is rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.62,
          "end": 75.67,
          "en": "So even if an item is not currently on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.67,
          "end": 77.72,
          "en": "like this last list item here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.72,
          "end": 81.12,
          "en": "this item is still rendered behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.12,
          "end": 83.78999999999999,
          "en": "even though it's not visible yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.78999999999999,
          "end": 87.87,
          "en": "Because ScrollView renders all its child items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.87,
          "end": 92.87,
          "en": "no matter if we're talking about 10, 20, or 10,000 items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.91,
          "end": 98.58,
          "en": "And for very long list, this can become a performance issue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.58,
          "end": 100.22999999999999,
          "en": "If you have a long list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.22999999999999,
          "end": 103.62,
          "en": "with dozens or hundreds or thousands of items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.62,
          "end": 105.77000000000001,
          "en": "rendering them all at the beginning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.77000000000001,
          "end": 109.87,
          "en": "even though vast majority is not even visible to the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.87,
          "end": 111.78999999999999,
          "en": "will slow down the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.78999999999999,
          "end": 114.62,
          "en": "And of course, that's not something we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.62,
          "end": 118.71000000000001,
          "en": "Therefore ScrollView is great for limited amounts of content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.71000000000001,
          "end": 122.55,
          "en": "like an article which has a fixed end at some point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.55,
          "end": 126.26,
          "en": "But for dynamic lists, which could become super long.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.26,
          "end": 128.67,
          "en": "We typical don't wanna use ScrollView.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.67,
          "end": 131.34,
          "en": "We can, but we typically don't want to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.34,
          "end": 134.89,
          "en": "to avoid possible performance issues.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.89,
          "end": 137.68,
          "en": "A better solution for such scenarios",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.68,
          "end": 142.23,
          "en": "is another built-in component that ships with React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.23,
          "end": 144.433,
          "en": "the FlatList component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.43,
          "end": 149.74,
          "en": "this is another component that will help scrolling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.74,
          "end": 151.61,
          "en": "But as the name suggests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.61,
          "end": 155.18,
          "en": "it's specifically built for scrollable lists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.18,
          "end": 158.15,
          "en": "And internally, it will only render the items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.15,
          "end": 159.77,
          "en": "that are actually visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.77,
          "end": 162.63,
          "en": "And all the items that are off screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.63,
          "end": 166.21,
          "en": "will only be loaded and rendered lazily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.21,
          "end": 169.563,
          "en": "as they are needed because the user is scrolling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.89,
          "end": 175.26,
          "en": "Now, internally, FlatList will have a small threshold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.26,
          "end": 179.05,
          "en": "to make sure it already starts loading and rendering items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.05,
          "end": 181.26,
          "en": "before they are visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.26,
          "end": 185.16,
          "en": "But it will only render them as the user gets closer to them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.16,
          "end": 188.13,
          "en": "as he or she is scrolling the list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.13,
          "end": 190.56,
          "en": "If you have 1000 items in your list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.56,
          "end": 193.65,
          "en": "the vast majority of items will not be loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 193.65,
          "end": 196.663,
          "en": "and will not be rendered when using FlatList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.02,
          "end": 200.653,
          "en": "So how do we with FlatList then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.9,
          "end": 206.9,
          "en": "Well, you do use it by replacing ScrollView with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.44,
          "end": 210.603,
          "en": "So we replace ScrollView with FlatList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 212.57999999999998,
          "end": 217.29,
          "en": "Now, regarding this alwaysBounceVertical prop here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.29,
          "end": 218.77,
          "en": "this is still supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 218.77,
          "end": 222.91,
          "en": "So you can leave it there because FlatList actually supports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.91,
          "end": 226.86,
          "en": "pretty much all of the props ScrollView supports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.86,
          "end": 230.9,
          "en": "Because internally it kind of has a similar implementation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 230.9,
          "end": 232.62,
          "en": "but with this optimization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.62,
          "end": 234.823,
          "en": "of only loading data when it's needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.01,
          "end": 238.99,
          "en": "So this is a first step, but we're not finished yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.99,
          "end": 241.803,
          "en": "We replace ScrollView with FlatList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.86,
          "end": 246.11,
          "en": "The next step is that we get rid of our custom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.11,
          "end": 248.75,
          "en": "mapping code here, we remove that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.75,
          "end": 251.623,
          "en": "we no longer map our data manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.76,
          "end": 256.66,
          "en": "Instead, we now have to pass this task to FlatList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.66,
          "end": 260.04,
          "en": "so that it can render this list efficiently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 260.04,
          "end": 262.78,
          "en": "by only rendering what's needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.78,
          "end": 264.59,
          "en": "FlatList is now in charge of this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.59,
          "end": 267.92,
          "en": "hence we need to let FlatList do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 267.92,
          "end": 272.92,
          "en": "And this is done by giving FlatList two important props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 273.95,
          "end": 277.363,
          "en": "The first one is the data prop, which is a required prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 278.21,
          "end": 281.05,
          "en": "This is a prop that points at the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 281.05,
          "end": 282.943,
          "en": "that should be output in this list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 284.26,
          "end": 288.48,
          "en": "In our example here, that would be the courseGoals array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 288.48,
          "end": 290.93,
          "en": "That's the data that should be output as a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 290.93,
          "end": 293.64300000000003,
          "en": "so we pass this as a value to data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 294.72,
          "end": 296.63,
          "en": "But that doesn't tell FlatList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 296.63,
          "end": 298.82,
          "en": "how the data should be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 298.82,
          "end": 302.32,
          "en": "You don't tell FlatList by passing content like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 302.32,
          "end": 304.41,
          "en": "between the opening and closing text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 304.41,
          "end": 306.403,
          "en": "that's not how we use FlatList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 307.86,
          "end": 309.95,
          "en": "Instead, we should cut this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.95,
          "end": 313.403,
          "en": "and we can turn FlatList into a self-closing component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 314.42,
          "end": 316.97,
          "en": "And we add another key prop now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 316.97,
          "end": 321.253,
          "en": "and that's another required prop, the renderItem prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 322.32,
          "end": 325.55,
          "en": "This is a prop that wants a function as a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 325.55,
          "end": 328.16,
          "en": "a function that will tell FlatList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 328.16,
          "end": 331.093,
          "en": "how to render the individual data items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 332.27,
          "end": 333.8,
          "en": "Therefore it is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 333.8,
          "end": 335.73,
          "en": "that will receive the individual item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 335.73,
          "end": 338.063,
          "en": "as a parameter, automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 338.94,
          "end": 341.3,
          "en": "FlatList will pass in this item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 341.3,
          "end": 343.15999999999997,
          "en": "whenever it calls this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 343.15999999999997,
          "end": 344.69,
          "en": "and it will call this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 344.69,
          "end": 348.15,
          "en": "whenever it determines that a new item must be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 348.15,
          "end": 350.07,
          "en": "because the user is scrolling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 350.07,
          "end": 352.313,
          "en": "and a new item should be made visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 353.2,
          "end": 354.92,
          "en": "And therefore, in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 354.92,
          "end": 357.44,
          "en": "in this array function which I defined here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 357.44,
          "end": 360.19,
          "en": "you then return to JSX code that should be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 360.19,
          "end": 362.18,
          "en": "for a given item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 362.18,
          "end": 365.47,
          "en": "Now, of course, we wanna output our item data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 365.47,
          "end": 368.1,
          "en": "and we received this item parameter value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 368.1,
          "end": 370.69,
          "en": "automatically by FlatList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 370.69,
          "end": 372.6,
          "en": "But this item which we get here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 372.6,
          "end": 377.09,
          "en": "is actually an object generated by FlatList internally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 377.09,
          "end": 381.02,
          "en": "An object that is wrapped around the individual data items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 381.02,
          "end": 383.46,
          "en": "we have in our data array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 383.46,
          "end": 385.64,
          "en": "And therefore I will actually name this itemData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 385.64,
          "end": 387.4,
          "en": "because it's actually an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 387.4,
          "end": 390.58,
          "en": "that does not just contain our values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 390.58,
          "end": 392.063,
          "en": "but also some metadata.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 393.3,
          "end": 395.61,
          "en": "Now, itemData does for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 395.61,
          "end": 398.46,
          "en": "also give us access to a index property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 398.46,
          "end": 400.59000000000003,
          "en": "Again, this object with this property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 400.59000000000003,
          "end": 402.88,
          "en": "is generated by FlatList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 402.88,
          "end": 404.01,
          "en": "And this holds the index",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 404.01,
          "end": 406.59000000000003,
          "en": "of the different items that are rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 406.59000000000003,
          "end": 408.84000000000003,
          "en": "First item here has an index of zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 408.84000000000003,
          "end": 411.603,
          "en": "the second item has an index of one and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 412.48,
          "end": 414.87,
          "en": "But itemData also holds another property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 414.87,
          "end": 416.87,
          "en": "that's very important for us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 416.87,
          "end": 419.24,
          "en": "and that's the property I will output here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 419.24,
          "end": 421.453,
          "en": "the item property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 422.5,
          "end": 425.08,
          "en": "This will hold the actual data items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 425.08,
          "end": 427.97,
          "en": "one, for each list item that's being rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 427.97,
          "end": 430.04,
          "en": "So with itemData.item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 430.04,
          "end": 434.28,
          "en": "we get access to the different data items we have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 434.28,
          "end": 436.72,
          "en": "Now, with that, we can get rid of this key prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 436.72,
          "end": 439.51,
          "en": "because we're no longer mapping this list manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 439.51,
          "end": 442.303,
          "en": "and hence keys are no longer managed like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 443.26,
          "end": 445.24,
          "en": "We will come back to keys in a second",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 445.24,
          "end": 447.42,
          "en": "but for the moment we'll remove it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 447.42,
          "end": 450.48,
          "en": "And now I will reload the apps by pressing R here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 450.48,
          "end": 452.89300000000003,
          "en": "in the terminal with the terminal selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 454.5,
          "end": 458.36,
          "en": "And if I now add another new item here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 458.36,
          "end": 462.94,
          "en": "you will see it shows up and I can add multiple items here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 462.94,
          "end": 466.88,
          "en": "And if I add enough items to exceed this screen height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 466.88,
          "end": 470.34000000000003,
          "en": "So if I add more and more items here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 470.34000000000003,
          "end": 474.98,
          "en": "you will see that this list also is scrollable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 474.98,
          "end": 476.65999999999997,
          "en": "I can scroll here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 476.65999999999997,
          "end": 478.99,
          "en": "But you also see of course that I'm getting a warning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 478.99,
          "end": 481.86,
          "en": "I did get it right from the start actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 481.86,
          "end": 486.19,
          "en": "And the warning is the end, that I'm missing some keys here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 486.19,
          "end": 487.023,
          "en": "Because it's still a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 487.023,
          "end": 489.63,
          "en": "and therefore we still should add keys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 489.63,
          "end": 492.383,
          "en": "but we don't add them as we added them before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 493.63,
          "end": 495.52,
          "en": "Instead when using FlatList,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 495.52,
          "end": 500.09,
          "en": "there are two main ways of adding keys to these list items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 500.09,
          "end": 503.49,
          "en": "The first approach is to turn your data values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 503.49,
          "end": 506.84,
          "en": "from primitive values like strings as we have it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 506.84,
          "end": 510.36,
          "en": "into objects that have a key property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 510.36,
          "end": 511.81,
          "en": "And that's what I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 512.96,
          "end": 514.75,
          "en": "When I add a new courseGoal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 514.75,
          "end": 518.3,
          "en": "instead of just adding the entered text like this as a goal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 518.3,
          "end": 522.7,
          "en": "so as a plain string, I will wrap this into a object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 522.7,
          "end": 525.33,
          "en": "Where I, for example have a text property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 525.33,
          "end": 527.86,
          "en": "that the actual goal text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 527.86,
          "end": 531.4,
          "en": "but where I actually also add a key property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 531.4,
          "end": 533.313,
          "en": "which I set to a unique key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 534.55,
          "end": 537.23,
          "en": "Now, to generate a unique key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 537.23,
          "end": 542.15,
          "en": "I will actually use Math.random toString like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 542.15,
          "end": 544.86,
          "en": "Which is not really a unique key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 544.86,
          "end": 547.74,
          "en": "I could generate the same number twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 547.74,
          "end": 549.973,
          "en": "but it's good enough for this demo here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 551.32,
          "end": 554.16,
          "en": "And now with that every item in my course goals array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 554.16,
          "end": 555.9,
          "en": "is actually an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 555.9,
          "end": 559.283,
          "en": "an object with a text property and with a key property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 560.12,
          "end": 562.64,
          "en": "And the special thing is that FlatList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 562.64,
          "end": 566.35,
          "en": "will automatically look for such a key property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 566.35,
          "end": 569.52,
          "en": "So FlatList does work with primitive values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 569.52,
          "end": 571.04,
          "en": "in the data array as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 571.04,
          "end": 573.27,
          "en": "as you saw a couple of minutes ago.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 573.27,
          "end": 574.71,
          "en": "But it works even better,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 574.71,
          "end": 579.08,
          "en": "if your data in this data array is a list of objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 579.08,
          "end": 581.36,
          "en": "So if you have a list of objects as data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 581.36,
          "end": 583.85,
          "en": "and every object has a key property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 583.85,
          "end": 585.64,
          "en": "because then this key property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 585.64,
          "end": 587.61,
          "en": "will automatically be used as a key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 587.61,
          "end": 589.253,
          "en": "for the items that are rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 590.67,
          "end": 593.66,
          "en": "Now, that we turned our items into objects here though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 593.66,
          "end": 596.73,
          "en": "we have to make sure that when we access the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 596.73,
          "end": 598.92,
          "en": "that belongs to a single item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 598.92,
          "end": 602.393,
          "en": "we dive into the text property here on the item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 603.3,
          "end": 605.62,
          "en": "Because every item is now an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 605.62,
          "end": 608.81,
          "en": "with a text property, that's what we set up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 608.81,
          "end": 611.833,
          "en": "Hence we have to access this text property down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 613.566,
          "end": 614.44,
          "en": "And then with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 614.44,
          "end": 617.95,
          "en": "if we save this and again reload this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 619.07,
          "end": 622.76,
          "en": "and I now start adding items here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 622.76,
          "end": 627.3,
          "en": "you will see that now I can add items as many as I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 627.3,
          "end": 629.33,
          "en": "and I don't get this warning anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 629.33,
          "end": 631.33,
          "en": "And I got this strollable list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 631.33,
          "end": 633.24,
          "en": "And under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 633.24,
          "end": 636.11,
          "en": "only the items that are needed are being rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 636.11,
          "end": 638.87,
          "en": "and the other items will be loaded lazily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 638.87,
          "end": 641.18,
          "en": "as we scroll closer to them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 641.18,
          "end": 643.593,
          "en": "That's how this FlatList works now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 644.92,
          "end": 647.68,
          "en": "Now, if you don't have a property named key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 214,
          "start": 647.68,
          "end": 650.32,
          "en": "because you're maybe getting data from an API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 215,
          "start": 650.32,
          "end": 652.32,
          "en": "and you can't influence its shape,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 216,
          "start": 652.32,
          "end": 654.02,
          "en": "and you don't wanna transform it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 217,
          "start": 654.02,
          "end": 657.29,
          "en": "just because flat list needs that key property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 218,
          "start": 657.29,
          "end": 659.05,
          "en": "You also got an alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 219,
          "start": 659.05,
          "end": 662.353,
          "en": "to setting up such a key property in the input data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 220,
          "start": 663.62,
          "end": 665.88,
          "en": "Let's say this would be named ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 221,
          "start": 665.88,
          "end": 668.32,
          "en": "this would be a reasonable property name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 222,
          "start": 668.32,
          "end": 670.96,
          "en": "because this could be a unique ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 223,
          "start": 670.96,
          "end": 672.67,
          "en": "But it would be the wrong name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 224,
          "start": 672.67,
          "end": 677.55,
          "en": "because this list is not looking for an ID property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 225,
          "start": 677.55,
          "end": 679.283,
          "en": "but for a key property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 226,
          "start": 680.51,
          "end": 682.12,
          "en": "Now, of course we could transform it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 227,
          "start": 682.12,
          "end": 685.53,
          "en": "but if you don't wanna do that, you can go to your FlatList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 228,
          "start": 685.53,
          "end": 688.8,
          "en": "and you can add another prop to the FlatList component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 229,
          "start": 688.8,
          "end": 692.86,
          "en": "And that would be the keyExtractor prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 230,
          "start": 692.86,
          "end": 697.86,
          "en": "The keyExtractor prop wants a function as a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 231,
          "start": 699.33,
          "end": 701.75,
          "en": "for example, an inline arrow function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 232,
          "start": 701.75,
          "end": 703.91,
          "en": "But you could also define a function somewhere else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 233,
          "start": 703.91,
          "end": 706.053,
          "en": "and pass up a point or edit here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 234,
          "start": 707.49,
          "end": 708.53,
          "en": "And this is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 235,
          "start": 708.53,
          "end": 712.43,
          "en": "which will automatically receive two parameter values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 236,
          "start": 712.43,
          "end": 714.093,
          "en": "item and index.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 237,
          "start": 715.06,
          "end": 718.3,
          "en": "These two values will be provided by FlatList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 238,
          "start": 718.3,
          "end": 720.37,
          "en": "when it calls this function for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 239,
          "start": 720.37,
          "end": 722.46,
          "en": "And it will call this function for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 240,
          "start": 722.46,
          "end": 724.593,
          "en": "for every list item that's being rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 241,
          "start": 725.74,
          "end": 727.34,
          "en": "Now, the renderItem function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 242,
          "start": 727.34,
          "end": 730.22,
          "en": "is also called for every list item that's rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 243,
          "start": 730.22,
          "end": 731.67,
          "en": "But the renderItem function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 244,
          "start": 731.67,
          "end": 734.8,
          "en": "is responsible for generating in the JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 245,
          "start": 734.8,
          "end": 736.903,
          "en": "that should be rendered for every item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 246,
          "start": 738.116,
          "end": 739.86,
          "en": "KeyExtractor on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 247,
          "start": 739.86,
          "end": 743.95,
          "en": "this function is simply called to get a key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 248,
          "start": 743.95,
          "end": 745.04,
          "en": "out of every item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 249,
          "start": 745.04,
          "end": 747.15,
          "en": "which then under the hood will be attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 250,
          "start": 747.15,
          "end": 749.327,
          "en": "to the item by the FlatList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 251,
          "start": 750.23,
          "end": 752.95,
          "en": "And therefore here you should return the key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 252,
          "start": 752.95,
          "end": 756.64,
          "en": "And since you get the item as the first parameter value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 253,
          "start": 756.64,
          "end": 760.11,
          "en": "and since I know that every item for me is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 254,
          "start": 760.11,
          "end": 761.8,
          "en": "with an ID property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 255,
          "start": 761.8,
          "end": 765.58,
          "en": "And since I know that the ID property makes for a great key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 256,
          "start": 765.58,
          "end": 769.563,
          "en": "since it will be unique, I can return item.id here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 257,
          "start": 770.8,
          "end": 772.92,
          "en": "And with that, I simply tell FlatList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 258,
          "start": 772.92,
          "end": 777.09,
          "en": "how it gets to a unique key for every item it outputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 259,
          "start": 777.09,
          "end": 778.47,
          "en": "So with that, if I save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 260,
          "start": 778.47,
          "end": 781.563,
          "en": "and I then again, reload everything here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 261,
          "start": 782.58,
          "end": 787.58,
          "en": "If I again, learn React Native here, this works as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 262,
          "start": 789.05,
          "end": 790.693,
          "en": "And I don't get any warnings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 263,
          "start": 792.83,
          "end": 796.32,
          "en": "This off course, all the works here on Android",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 264,
          "start": 796.32,
          "end": 797.633,
          "en": "if you wanna see it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 265,
          "start": 798.74,
          "end": 801.31,
          "en": "I can add multiple goals there as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 266,
          "start": 801.31,
          "end": 803.353,
          "en": "and there it's also scrollable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 267,
          "start": 804.5,
          "end": 808,
          "en": "So that's FlatList and action, and you should use FlatList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 268,
          "start": 808,
          "end": 810.65,
          "en": "whenever you have lists with dynamic data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 269,
          "start": 810.65,
